From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:00:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] GLSL: Keep forwarded copies of access chains as access
 chains.

OpCopyObject of an access chain pointer forwarded the expression but
lost the access chain flag, so should_dereference() saw a plain pointer
value and a store through the copy came out as *_33[i] = x, which does
not compile. DXIL bitcasts of group shared pointers produce this.
---
 spirv_glsl.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spirv_glsl.cpp b/spirv_glsl.cpp
index c8284a21..d5ca9e68 100644
--- a/spirv_glsl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_glsl.cpp
@@ -13988,6 +13988,11 @@ void CompilerGLSL::emit_instruction(const Instruction &instruction)
 			{
 				e.implied_read_expressions = rhs_expr->implied_read_expressions;
 				e.expression_dependencies = rhs_expr->expression_dependencies;
+
+				// A forwarded copy of an access chain still names the object, it is not a pointer value.
+				// Otherwise a store through the copy gets dereferenced, e.g. *_33[i] = x.
+				if (pointer && rhs_expr->access_chain && expression_is_forwarded(id))
+					e.access_chain = true;
 			}
 		}
 		break;
